{"cell": "npo-gpt-oss-20b__bbh", "question_id": "bbh::web_of_lies::194", "benchmark": "bbh", "domain": "M", "question": "Question: Raymond lies. Fletcher says Raymond lies. Amberly says Fletcher lies. Shenna says Amberly tells the truth. Dallas says Shenna tells the truth. Does Dallas tell the truth?", "segments": [{"seg_id": 0, "text": "We have a logic puzzle."}, {"seg_id": 1, "text": "We have five people: Raymond, Fletcher, Amberly, Shenna, Dallas."}, {"seg_id": 2, "text": "Each person either tells truth or lies."}, {"seg_id": 3, "text": "We have statements:"}, {"seg_id": 4, "text": "1."}, {"seg_id": 5, "text": "Raymond says: \"Raymond lies.\" So Raymond says \"Raymond lies.\" That is a statement about himself."}, {"seg_id": 6, "text": "So if Raymond is truthful, then his statement \"Raymond lies\" would be true, but that would mean Raymond lies, contradiction."}, {"seg_id": 7, "text": "So Raymond cannot be truthful."}, {"seg_id": 8, "text": "If Raymond is lying, then his statement \"Raymond lies\" is false."}, {"seg_id": 9, "text": "That means Raymond does not lie, i.e., Raymond tells truth."}, {"seg_id": 10, "text": "Contradiction again?"}, {"seg_id": 11, "text": "Let's analyze carefully."}, {"seg_id": 12, "text": "Let R be truth value of Raymond (True if he tells truth)."}, {"seg_id": 13, "text": "Statement S_R: \"Raymond lies.\" That is equivalent to ¬R."}, {"seg_id": 14, "text": "So S_R is true iff ¬R."}, {"seg_id": 15, "text": "But S_R is the statement that Raymond says."}, {"seg_id": 16, "text": "If Raymond is truthful, then S_R must be true."}, {"seg_id": 17, "text": "So if R = True, then S_R true => ¬R true => R false."}, {"seg_id": 18, "text": "Contradiction."}, {"seg_id": 19, "text": "So R cannot be True."}, {"seg_id": 20, "text": "If R = False (Raymond lies), then S_R is false."}, {"seg_id": 21, "text": "But if R = False, then S_R is false."}, {"seg_id": 22, "text": "But S_R is the statement that Raymond says."}, {"seg_id": 23, "text": "If he lies, his statement is false."}, {"seg_id": 24, "text": "So S_R false is consistent."}, {"seg_id": 25, "text": "So R = False is consistent."}, {"seg_id": 26, "text": "So Raymond is a liar."}, {"seg_id": 27, "text": "Thus Raymond lies."}, {"seg_id": 28, "text": "2."}, {"seg_id": 29, "text": "Fletcher says Raymond lies."}, {"seg_id": 30, "text": "So Fletcher says \"Raymond lies.\" That statement is true because we found Raymond lies."}, {"seg_id": 31, "text": "So Fletcher's statement is true."}, {"seg_id": 32, "text": "So Fletcher is truthful."}, {"seg_id": 33, "text": "So F = True."}, {"seg_id": 34, "text": "3."}, {"seg_id": 35, "text": "Amberly says Fletcher lies."}, {"seg_id": 36, "text": "So Amberly says \"Fletcher lies.\" That statement is false because Fletcher is truthful."}, {"seg_id": 37, "text": "So Amberly's statement is false."}, {"seg_id": 38, "text": "So Amberly is liar."}, {"seg_id": 39, "text": "So A = False."}, {"seg_id": 40, "text": "4."}, {"seg_id": 41, "text": "Shenna says Amberly tells the truth."}, {"seg_id": 42, "text": "So Shenna says \"Amberly tells truth.\" That statement is false because Amberly is liar."}, {"seg_id": 43, "text": "So Shenna's statement is false."}, {"seg_id": 44, "text": "So Shenna is liar."}, {"seg_id": 45, "text": "So S = False."}, {"seg_id": 46, "text": "5."}, {"seg_id": 47, "text": "Dallas says Shenna tells the truth."}, {"seg_id": 48, "text": "So Dallas says \"Shenna tells truth.\" That statement is false because Shenna is liar."}, {"seg_id": 49, "text": "So Dallas's statement is false."}, {"seg_id": 50, "text": "So Dallas is liar."}, {"seg_id": 51, "text": "So D = False."}, {"seg_id": 52, "text": "Thus Dallas tells the truth?"}, {"seg_id": 53, "text": "No, Dallas lies."}, {"seg_id": 54, "text": "So answer: No."}, {"seg_id": 55, "text": "Check consistency: All statements consistent."}, {"seg_id": 56, "text": "So answer: No."}, {"seg_id": 57, "text": "Thus concise answer: No."}], "events": [{"s": 6, "t": "subgoal_done", "a": "judge"}, {"s": 6, "t": "failed_attempt", "a": "regex"}, {"s": 7, "t": "backtrack", "a": "judge"}, {"s": 10, "t": "failed_attempt", "a": "judge"}, {"s": 11, "t": "backtrack", "a": "judge"}, {"s": 18, "t": "failed_attempt", "a": "judge"}, {"s": 18, "t": "failed_attempt", "a": "regex"}, {"s": 19, "t": "backtrack", "a": "judge"}, {"s": 25, "t": "subgoal_done", "a": "judge"}, {"s": 26, "t": "subgoal_done", "a": "judge"}, {"s": 33, "t": "subgoal_done", "a": "judge"}, {"s": 39, "t": "subgoal_done", "a": "judge"}, {"s": 45, "t": "subgoal_done", "a": "judge"}, {"s": 51, "t": "subgoal_done", "a": "judge"}, {"s": 53, "t": "commit", "a": "judge"}, {"s": 54, "t": "commit", "a": "regex"}, {"s": 55, "t": "verify", "a": "judge"}, {"s": 56, "t": "commit", "a": "regex"}, {"s": 57, "t": "commit", "a": "regex"}], "spans": [{"a": 0, "b": 5, "op": "SETUP"}, {"a": 5, "b": 19, "op": "EXPLORING"}, {"a": 19, "b": 52, "op": "DERIVING"}, {"a": 52, "b": 58, "op": "CONCLUDING"}], "agents": ["regex", "judge"], "lam": [0.532, 0.532, 0.532, 0.532, 0.532, 0.532, 0.532, 0.856, 0.765, 0.583, 0.543, 0.697, 0.73, 0.575, 0.541, 0.534, 0.532, 0.532, 0.532, 0.856, 0.765, 0.583, 0.543, 0.534, 0.532, 0.532, 0.694, 0.729, 0.575, 0.541, 0.534, 0.532, 0.532, 0.532, 0.694, 0.567, 0.539, 0.533, 0.532, 0.532, 0.694, 0.567, 0.539, 0.533, 0.532, 0.532, 0.694, 0.567, 0.539, 0.533, 0.532, 0.532, 0.694, 0.567, 0.702, 0.731, 0.737, 0.739], "corpus": "native_po_2026_08_11", "trace_model": "openai/gpt-oss-20b", "tag": "gptoss20", "model_label": "gpt-oss-20b", "correct": true, "cap": 8192, "arm": "none"}